<p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> Kale indoors is doable, but you have to respect its quirks. Cool temperatures. Moderate, consistent light. Harvest the outer leaves. Water with cold water once a week to keep them sweet. It took me 2 killed batches and $50 in wasted supplies to figure that out. Now I have a steady supply from one pot in my kitchen corner. If you want to try it, <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=LED+grow+light+panel+100W+for+indoor+plants&tag=tabletopharve-20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored">check current light prices on Amazon</a>. Mine was $45 when I bought it, but it fluctuates between $38-50. If it is under $42, grab it.</p>

